## Anti-Aliasing Techniques

### 1. Multiple Bandlimited Tables
- Pre-compute tables for different frequency ranges
- Higher-frequency tables have fewer harmonics
- Linear crossfade between adjacent tables

### 2. PolyBLEP (Polynomial Bandlimited Step)
```cpp
float polyBLEP(float t, float dt)
{
    // t is the phase, dt is the phase increment
    if (t < dt)
    {
        // Rising edge
        t /= dt;
        return t * t * (0.5f - t);
    }
    else if (t > 1.0f - dt)
    {
        // Falling edge
        t = (t - 1.0f) / dt;
        return t * t * (0.5f + t);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

### 3. Antiderivative Anti-Aliasing (ADAA)
- Modern approach using IIR filters
- Up to order 16 anti-aliasing
- SIMD optimization available

## JUCE Implementation

```cpp
class WavetableSynthVoice : public SynthesiserVoice
{
public:
    void noteOn(int midiNote, float velocity) override
    {
