```

## Best Practices

1. **Table size**: 2048-4096 samples provides good quality/performance balance
2. **Number of tables**: 8-16 tables for smooth transitions
3. **Interpolation**: Linear is fast; Hermite or cubic for higher quality
4. **Memory**: Store tables as floats; consider SIMD alignment
5. **Phase precision**: Use double for phase accumulator to avoid drift

## Common Waveforms

| Waveform | Harmonic Spectrum | Notes |
|----------|------------------|-------|
| Sine | Fundamental only | No aliasing needed |
| Sawtooth | All harmonics, 1/n | Most aliasing-prone |
| Square | Odd harmonics, 1/n | Moderate aliasing |
| Triangle | Odd harmonics, 1/n² | Least aliasing-prone |
| PWM | Variable width | Two tables with phase offset |

